  "details": "Discovered this when a post-build callback method would only work correctly when there was a successful build despite me handling cases when there wasn't (via OnSdkBuildError).\n\n \n\n---\n\nRepro:\n\n1. Build a .vrcw bundle successfully, at least once\n\n2. Create a callback method for OnSdkBuildError\n\n3. Simulate a scenario where the asset bundle would fail to build\n\n4. Attempt to build\n\nResult: If the scene name hasn't changed / an existing asset bundle exists in AppData, it will always fire the OnSdkBuildSuccess event. If you delete the .vrcw file + rebuild - it will appropriately fire the 'OnSdkBuildError' event.\n\nScope: \n\nBesides affecting those with previously successful builds - this likely could affect those who use the same scene names across multiple projects because they'd share the same `scene-<target>-<scene-name.vrcw` format.\n\nUnity 2022.3.6f1\n\nSDK: 3.5.0\n\nlove u",
